From 3ae0049380fefea2f27905663c8ea7031ce801c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Bowman-Matthews <josh@joshmatthews.net>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] script: Ensure pending timer callbacks are always
 reachable from GC roots. (#48548)

The timer code contained crown warning suppressions that hid the
presence of unrooted callbacks after #48315. These changes address that
by adding rooted versions of several enums that can be passed around
safely as arguments and used when invoking the timer callbacks, and by
ensuring that the unrooted versions receive appropriate crown
annotations so we can't reintroduce similar issues in the future.

The changes that split the JS timer callbacks out from the non-JS timers
prevent callers that only care about non-JS timers from having to think
about rooting.

Testing: New crashtest added.
Fixes: #48538
Closes #48545
Fixes: #20452

---------

Signed-off-by: Josh Matthews <josh@joshmatthews.net>
